---
import { commands } from '../../data/commands';
---

<section id="get-started" class="page-section install-section">
  <div class="install-card">
    <div class="install-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow">04 / Your terminal</div>
      <h2>Small setup.<br /><em>Big collection.</em></h2>
      <p>PokéCatch runs locally on Python 3.12+. Install it with pipx, then start with a clean inventory and 50 Poké Balls.</p>
      <div class="install-notes"><span>✓ Python 3.12+</span><span>✓ Saves to <code>~/.pokecatch</code></span><span>✓ Open source game loop</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="install-terminal mockup-code">
      <pre data-prefix="$"><code>pipx install pokecatch-cli-game</code></pre>
      <pre data-prefix="$"><code>pokecatch hunt</code></pre>
      <pre data-prefix=""><code>Wild encounter found.</code></pre>
      <pre data-prefix="$"><code>pokecatch catch pb</code></pre>
      <pre data-prefix=""><code>Catch attempt resolved.</code></pre>
      <div class="terminal-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="command-reference" aria-label="PokéCatch command reference">
    <div class="command-reference-head">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">04A / Command deck</div>
        <h3>Every command in your kit.</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Run <code>--help</code> at the top level or after a subcommand. PokéCatch is local and stateful: inventory, stats, and store displays load the player save.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="command-syntax">
      <span>GENERAL SYNTAX</span>
      <code>pokecatch &lt;command&gt; [arguments] [options]</code>
      <code>python -m pokecatch &lt;command&gt; [arguments] [options]</code>
    </div>
    <div class="command-table-wrap">
      <table class="command-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Alias</th><th>Purpose / effects</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {commands.map((item) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>pokecatch {item.command}</code></th>
              <td>{item.alias}</td>
              <td>{item.purpose}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="command-note">Catch accepts canonical ball names or lowercase aliases such as <code>pb</code>, <code>net</code>, and <code>mb</code>. Parser errors reject unknown arguments and invalid purchase quantities.</p>
  </div>
</section>
